{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1784712190","published":"2026-10-18T22:57:31Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:32:05.623723219Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-42533","CVE-2026-60005"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-42533, CVE-2026-60005","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in nginx worker via map+regex\n     capture variables in script engine\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-42533.patch: backport upstream commits\n       ea47fabf55e2 (Script: simplified copy capture codes),\n       7ac67898bdfe (Script: buffer overrun protection),\n       326b17b00383 (Script: buffer overrun protection in direct script\n       usage), 78950bdcd443 (Access log: buffer overrun protection),\n       b99f804ad38a (Fixed uninitialized memory read caused by stale regex\n       captures), and 97e40e59b7b4 (Script: avoid garbage at the end of\n       the result string); add e->end pointer and\n       ngx_http_script_check_length() guard to all script copy code paths,\n       reset r->ncaptures on regex reallocation, and thread params_len /\n       headers_len through fastcgi, grpc, scgi, uwsgi upstream request\n       builders so an attacker-controlled map+regex expansion can no\n       longer overrun the assembled request or access log buffer\n     - CVE-2026-42533","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libnginx-mod-http-auth-pam","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:20.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libnginx-mod-http-auth-pam?distro=ubuntu-20.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.18.0-0ubuntu1.7+tuxcare.els7"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu20.04els/CLSA-2026-1784712190.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libnginx-mod-http-cache-purge","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:20.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libnginx-mod-http-cache-purge?distro=ubuntu-20.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.18.0-0ubuntu1.7+tuxcare.els7"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github